    "no": "001",
    "identity": "Field Brief",
    "theme": "allocation",
    "phrase": "Scarcity & allocation",
    "seed": 2366840543,
    "framing": "The dominant thread is the collision between AI expansion and public policy. Three of today's five developments concern governments deciding who bears the electricity, water, security, and fiscal costs associated with rapidly changing technologies and federal policy. AI policy is rapidly expanding beyond algorithms into the physical economy that supports them. Texas and California are both wrestling with electricity capacity, water scarcity, and cost allocation; EPA is simultaneously changing the federal regulatory environment governing the generators that may supply some of that incremental electricity; and governments internationally are negotiating rules for AI's highest-risk military applications. For environmental economics, the data-center story is especially revealing: it is becoming a real-world case study in externalities, congestion, incidence, infrastructure cost allocation, resource scarcity, and state-level regulatory competition — all generated by a very large positive demand shock for electricity and water.",
    "frozen": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 600 800\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Field Brief, issue 001: Scarcity &amp; allocation\"><title>Field Brief · 001 · Scarcity &amp; allocation</title><desc>Conceptual issue illustration derived from the current edition’s framing; not a measured result.</desc><rect width=\"600\" height=\"800\" fill=\"#f1e6d0\"/><g><path d=\"M92 104V480H522\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#221a14\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M115 158L500 425M115 425L500 158\" stroke=\"#8a2a36\" stroke-width=\"9\"/><path d=\"M160 300H460\" stroke=\"#221a14\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"307\" cy=\"291\" r=\"48\" fill=\"#c5ad88\" stroke=\"#221a14\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><path d=\"M42 570H558\" stroke=\"#221a14\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g fill=\"#221a14\"><text x=\"42\" y=\"634\" font-family=\"Instrument Serif,Georgia,serif\" font-size=\"48\">Field Brief</text><text x=\"42\" y=\"683\" font-family=\"IBM Plex Sans Condensed, sans-serif\" font-size=\"19\" letter-spacing=\"2\">ISSUE 001 / 2026-09-26</text><text x=\"42\" y=\"740\" font-family=\"Instrument Serif,Georgia,serif\" font-size=\"26\">Scarcity &amp; allocation</text></g></svg>"
