    "framing": "Econometrics You estimate a two-group, two-period difference-in-differences model. Before treatment, the treated-group mean is 12 and the control-group mean is 10. After treatment, the treated-group mean is 17 and the control-group mean is 13. Under parallel trends, what is the estimated treatment effect? Difference-in-differences Parallel trends The treated group rises by 5 and the control group rises by 3. Difference-in-differences is 5 − 3 = 2. Parallel trends supplies the untreated counterfactual change for the treated group. Microeconomics A competitive market has inverse demand P = 100 − Q and inverse supply P = 20 + Q. The government imposes a binding price ceiling of $50. Which statements are correct? Price ceilings Market disequilibrium At P = 50, demand gives Q = 50 and supply gives Q = 30, so the shortage is 20. The unconstrained equilibrium is Q = 40 and P = 60, so the ceiling binds. Environmental economics Two firms must jointly abate 10 units. Firm A has MAC A = 2a A ; firm B has MAC B = 6a B . What cost-effective allocation satisfies a A + a B = 10? Cost-effective abatement Equimarginal principle Cost effectiveness requires equal marginal abatement costs: 2a A = 6a B , so a A = 3a B . Combining with total abatement of 10 gives a B = 2.5 and a A = 7.5. Causal inference True or false: instrument relevance by itself is enough to justify a causal interpretation of an instrumental-variables coefficient. Instrumental variables Exclusion restriction Relevance False. Relevance only requires that the instrument shifts treatment. A causal interpretation also requires assumptions such as exogeneity/independence and exclusion; LATE additionally uses monotonicity. Macroeconomics The nominal interest rate is 6% and expected inflation is 2%. Using the Fisher approximation, what is the expected real interest rate? Fisher equation Real interest rate Using r ≈ i − Eπ gives 6% − 2% = 4%. The exact Fisher relation gives a value close to 3.92%. Statistics & inference You increase sample size from 400 to 1,600 while keeping the data-generating process and estimator otherwise unchanged. Under standard regularity conditions, which statements are generally correct? Sampling variance Standard errors Asymptotics Standard errors commonly scale with 1/√n, so quadrupling n halves the standard error and quarters the variance. Confidence intervals narrow. Larger samples do not automatically remove bias from misspecification, measurement error or non-random sampling. Resource economics A renewable resource follows G(X) = 0.5X(1 − X/800). What is maximum sustainable yield? Logistic growth Maximum sustainable yield Maximum sustainable yield occurs at K/2 = 400. Growth there is rK/4 = 0.5 × 800 / 4 = 100. This is a biological benchmark, not necessarily the profit-maximizing stock. Research design A researcher evaluates job training using observational data. Participants had substantially lower earnings than nonparticipants for several years before enrollment. After matching only on age, sex and education, the researcher reports the post-program earnings gap as causal. What is the main concern? Selection on observables Pre-treatment outcomes Conditional independence Persistent pre-treatment earnings differences indicate that participants and controls differ along dimensions related to future earnings. Matching only on demographics leaves important selection concerns. More observations reduce sampling noise, not selection bias, and the bias direction is not determined here.",
    "frozen": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 600 800\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The Workbook, set 003: Comparisons &amp; evidence\"><title>The Workbook · 003 · Comparisons &amp; evidence</title><desc>Conceptual issue illustration derived from the current edition’s framing; not a measured result.</desc><rect width=\"600\" height=\"800\" fill=\"#f7f7f3\"/><g><path d=\"M60 60H540M60 120H540M60 180H540M60 240H540M60 300H540M60 360H540M60 420H540M60 480H540M60 60V500M120 60V500M180 60V500M240 60V500M300 60V500M360 60V500M420 60V500M480 60V500M540 60V500\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1c2f4a\" opacity=\".12\"/><path d=\"M92 104V480H522\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1c2f4a\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M110 432L210 367L310 301L481 164\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0e5360\" stroke-width=\"12\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M110 432L210 367L310 301L481 283\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1c2f4a\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-dasharray=\"10 8\"/><path d=\"M310 126V480\" stroke=\"#1c2f4a\" opacity=\".35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M481 164V283\" stroke=\"#b5ced1\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"310\" cy=\"301\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1c2f4a\"/></g><path d=\"M42 570H558\" stroke=\"#1c2f4a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g fill=\"#1c2f4a\"><text x=\"42\" y=\"634\" font-family=\"STIX Two Text,Georgia,serif\" font-size=\"48\">The Workbook</text><text x=\"42\" y=\"683\" font-family=\"IBM Plex Sans Condensed, sans-serif\" font-size=\"19\" letter-spacing=\"2\">SET 003 / 2026-09-30</text><text x=\"42\" y=\"740\" font-family=\"STIX Two Text,Georgia,serif\" font-size=\"26\">Comparisons &amp; evidence</text></g></svg>"
